{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2198-01-31 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I'm Dr. Lee. You were brought in this morning because of vomiting. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2198-01-31 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I woke up at 4 a.m. with sudden nausea and started vomiting. I’ve done it about 10 times since then. It’s just like my last episode."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2198-01-31 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Was there any blood in the vomit?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2198-01-31 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not really blood, but there was some dark, coffee-ground-looking stuff in it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2198-01-31 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. That can happen with stomach irritation. You had a Botox injection in your esophagus a week ago, right? And your gastric pacer was adjusted?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2198-01-31 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. I felt better for a few days, then this hit me out of nowhere."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2198-01-31 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s consistent with your gastroparesis flaring up again. We’ll keep you here because you can’t keep anything down. We’ve started IV fluids and anti-nausea meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2198-01-31 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be able to eat soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2198-01-31 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We need to let your stomach rest. Once the vomiting stops, we’ll try small sips, then advance slowly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2198-01-31 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2198-01-31 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an X-ray of your abdomen to check for a blockage. Good news — there’s no obstruction. Your gastric pacer is in place and looks stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2198-01-31 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not broken?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2198-01-31 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it’s working fine. This is more about your stomach not moving food properly, which is part of your diabetes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2198-01-31 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2198-01-31 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure was high this morning, likely from pain and vomiting. We gave you a medication to bring it down, and it’s improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2198-01-31 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had high blood pressure before. Is it a concern?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2198-01-31 14:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re watching it. We’ll switch you to your usual blood pressure pill tomorrow if it stays under control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2198-01-31 14:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I take lisinopril at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2198-01-31 14:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll restart that. Your diabetes is also being managed with your usual insulin — glargine at night and sliding scale for meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2198-01-31 18:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2198-01-31 18:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still nauseous, but not vomiting as much. The IV meds are helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2198-01-31 18:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. We’ll keep the IV fluids going and monitor your labs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2198-02-01 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your white blood cell count was a bit high yesterday, but it’s coming down. That’s a sign your body isn’t fighting a serious infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2198-02-01 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had a urine test — was there an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2198-02-01 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The culture showed mixed bacteria, but it looks like contamination from skin. No treatment needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2198-02-01 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I was worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2198-02-01 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to try giving you small sips of water. If you keep that down, we can move to clear liquids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2198-02-01 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great! I’m ready to try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2198-02-02 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well overnight — no vomiting. We’re advancing you to a soft diet. Start with small bites and chew well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2198-02-02 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great news. Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2198-02-02 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We want to make sure you can keep food and your medications down for a full day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2198-02-02 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood sugar has been stable on your home insulin plan. The endocrine team reviewed and agrees it’s appropriate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2198-02-02 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I don’t want to change my routine if it’s working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2198-02-03 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did another abdominal X-ray yesterday to check for ileus. It was clear — no blockage or slow transit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2198-02-03 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So my stomach is just slow, not blocked?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2198-02-03 08:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. That’s gastroparesis. We’re adding metoclopramide — Reglan — to help speed things up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2198-02-03 08:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve taken that before. Does it have side effects?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2198-02-03 08:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sometimes it can cause restlessness, but we’ll start low and watch you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2198-02-04 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve made great progress. You’re eating soft food, keeping meds down, and not vomiting. We’re planning for discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2198-02-04 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s wonderful! What about my medications?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2198-02-04 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll go home with your insulin, plus new prescriptions: Reglan for stomach emptying, Protonix for acid reflux, Zofran for nausea as needed, and lisinopril for blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2198-02-04 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll take them as directed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2198-02-04 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One thing — your sodium level is low, 130. But you’re not having symptoms like dizziness, so it’s mild."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2198-02-04 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I worry?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2198-02-04 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. But if you feel lightheaded or confused, seek care. We want you to get a blood test next week to check it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2198-02-04 14:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to do that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2198-02-05 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. You can go home today. Make sure to follow up with your gastroenterologist — they may check your gastric pacer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2198-02-05 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I have an appointment scheduled."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2198-02-05 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Take your new meds, stay hydrated, and call if nausea returns or you feel unwell."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2198-02-05 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2198-02-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing — your discharge papers say to draw labs next week. Please call your PCP with the results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2198-02-05 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2198-02-05 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re finalizing your discharge. Any last questions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2198-02-05 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I think I understand everything. Thanks for your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2198-02-05 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care and get some rest at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2198-02-05 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming — you’ve tolerated breakfast and your pills. You’re cleared to leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2198-02-05 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2198-02-05 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Here’s your prescription list and lab slip. Please follow up as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2198-02-05 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2198-02-05 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll see you only if you need us."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2198-01-31 08:54:00",
    "admission_end": "2198-02-05 14:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 30-year-old woman with Type 1 diabetes and a history of gastroparesis s/p gastric pacer presented with acute nausea and vomiting, one week after a prior hospitalization for similar symptoms. She had recently received a Botox injection for gastroparesis and reported coffee-ground emesis. She was admitted for inability to tolerate oral intake and managed with IV fluids, antiemetics (ondansetron, metoclopramide, compazine), and proton pump inhibition. Her hypertension, exacerbated by vomiting and anxiety, was controlled with IV metoprolol and transitioned to oral lisinopril. Abdominal imaging showed no obstruction or ileus. She gradually improved, tolerating a soft diet and oral medications. Her sodium was noted to be low (130) on discharge but asymptomatic; outpatient labs were ordered. She was discharged home in stable condition with new prescriptions for metoclopramide, pantoprazole, ondansetron, and lisinopril, and follow-up planned with gastroenterology for pacer evaluation.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], not stated as uncontrolled",
      "Hyposmolality and/or hyponatremia",
      "Persistent vomiting",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Esophagitis, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Leukocytosis, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
